TEST 13819 -- Classify traffic via Source/Destination IPv6 address
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22 09:50:10  tb470   policy ingress on port2.0.2
Method: the policy's ACTION is `set dscp 46`, so a MATCH is decoded at
egress as dscp 46 and a non-match keeps its original marking. Matching is
measured on the wire, not inferred from a counter.

--- baseline, no policy ---
  IPv6 src in matched /64    got=8 dscp=[0]
  IPv6 src elsewhere         got=8 dscp=[0]

configure terminal
Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
IE520-stk(config)#ipv6 access-list qacl6
IE520-stk(config-ipv6-hw-acl)#permit ipv6 2001:db8:50::/64 any
IE520-stk(config-ipv6-hw-acl)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#class-map qcm
IE520-stk(config-cmap)#match access-group qacl6
IE520-stk(config-cmap)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#policy-map qpm
IE520-stk(config-pmap)#class qcm
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#set dscp 46
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#exit
IE520-stk(config-pmap)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#interface port2.0.2
IE520-stk(config-if)#service-policy input qpm
IE520-stk(config-if)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#end
